-- title:
--   Graph of a section: kernel pulls back to the section's kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, with associated projective Weierstrass model $\mathrm{projModelCR}\,W = \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded quotient of the polynomial ring in three variables over $T$ by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic, and with structure morphism $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,W : \mathrm{projModelCR}\,W \to \operatorname{Spec} T$ given by $\operatorname{Proj}$'s canonical morphism to the spectrum of the degree-zero part followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $T \to (\text{degree-}0\text{ part})$. Let $R$ be a section, that is, a pair consisting of a morphism $R.1 : \operatorname{Spec} T \to \mathrm{projModelCR}\,W$ together with a proof $R.2$ that $R.1$ followed by $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,W$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} T$. Form `graphOver`, the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} T \to \mathrm{projModelCR}\,W \times_{\operatorname{Spec} T} \operatorname{Spec} T$ (fibre product of $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,W$ with the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} T$) obtained by lifting $R.1$ and $\mathrm{id}$, and `toPullbackId`, the morphism $\mathrm{projModelCR}\,W \to \mathrm{projModelCR}\,W \times_{\operatorname{Spec} T} \operatorname{Spec} T$ obtained by lifting $\mathrm{id}$ and $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,W$. The assertion is that the comap along `toPullbackId` of the kernel ideal sheaf of `graphOver` equals the kernel ideal sheaf of $R.1$ on $\mathrm{projModelCR}\,W$.
--
--   This identifies, on the projective Weierstrass model itself, the ideal sheaf cutting out a section with the ideal sheaf of its graph inside the fibre product taken along the identity; it is the bookkeeping step that lets the divisor attached to a point be read off from the section. It is used in the global Drinfeld-basis material, for the statements on unit multiples of the relevant power series and on the comparison of torsion ideals with basis divisors.
